# Set the AE (auto exposure) maximum exposure time limit.
#
# Sends AE opcode 0x26. This limit is the upper clamp that the device's
# automatic exposure convergence loop is allowed to use, so it takes effect
# in AUTO mode (it does not switch AE into manual mode).
#
# Unit: milliseconds. Device-enforced minimum is 5.0 ms; values below that
# are rejected with rc=403 (parameter out of range). The limit should stay
# below the frame period (at dtof_fps=290 the period is ~34 ms, so 33.0 ms
# is a practical ceiling).
#
# A shorter limit reduces motion blur in fast-motion scenes but darkens dim
# scenes. There is no SDK getter for this value; query the AE stream state
# via /odin1/get_ae instead.
float32 max_exposure_ms
---
bool success
int32 rc                # 0=ok, >0=device error (400..405 or 0xFF), <0=SDK error
